{# Engraved mark.

   Stroke, never fill. A solid glyph reads as a UI affordance; a stroked one at
   1.5px reads as line work cut at the same weight as the guilloche, which is
   the only reason this world tolerates icons at all.

   Decorative by default: aria-hidden with no label, because it always sits
   beside a heading that already says the same thing. Pass `iconLabel` only
   where the icon is the sole carrier of meaning, which on this site is nowhere
   yet.

   Usage:
     {% set iconName = "handshake" %}
     {% include "components/icon.njk" %}

   vector-effect keeps the stroke at 1.5px when the SVG is scaled, so a 40px
   mark and a 20px mark are cut with the same tool. #}
{%- set i = icons[iconName] -%}
{%- if i %}
<svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24" height="24"
     fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"
     stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"
     vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke"
     {% if iconLabel %}role="img" aria-label="{{ iconLabel }}"{% else %}aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"{% endif %}>
  <path d="{{ i.path }}"></path>
</svg>
{%- endif -%}
